BT 0.5 0.5 0.5 rg /F1 8 Tf 425.28 815.00 Td (Team Srinathon | Hackathon 2026) Tj ET
0.93 0.95 0.98 rg 40.00 776.00 515.28 22.00 re f
0.1 0.3 0.65 rg 40.00 776.00 4.00 22.00 re f
BT 0.1 0.25 0.55 rg /F2 13 Tf 52.00 782.00 Td (5. The Three Guarantees, Formally Argued) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.25 0.4 rg /F2 11 Tf 40.00 746.00 Td (1. Durability: Once ACK is sent, the data survives) Tj ET
0.75 0.8 0.85 rg 40.00 743.00 515.28 0.50 re f
BT 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg /F1 9.5 Tf 40.00 730.00 Td (Durability is enforced through a strict write-ordering protocol executed under a mutual-exclusion write) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg /F1 9.5 Tf 40.00 717.00 Td (lock. When put or batch is called, all record bytes are formatted into contiguous binary memory with) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg /F1 9.5 Tf 40.00 704.00 Td (their IEEE 802.3 CRC32 checksums and written to disk using synchronous fs.writeSync\(fd, buffer, 0, len,) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg /F1 9.5 Tf 40.00 691.00 Td (writeOffset\). Crucially, before returning success or emitting ACK <op-id> to stdout, the engine executes) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg /F1 9.5 Tf 40.00 678.00 Td (fs.fsyncSync\(fd\) \(which invokes FlushFileBuffers on Windows and fsync on POSIX\). This system call blocks) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg /F1 9.5 Tf 40.00 665.00 Td (execution until all drive caches and file system metadata have committed the bytes to persistent) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg /F1 9.5 Tf 40.00 652.00 Td (storage. Because ACK is only printed after fsyncSync returns successfully, any acknowledged operation is) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg /F1 9.5 Tf 40.00 639.00 Td (physically resident on disk and guaranteed to survive immediate process termination.) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.25 0.4 rg /F2 11 Tf 40.00 614.00 Td (2. Atomicity: A batch is never half visible) Tj ET
